---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import { agentTools } from "../../runtime/agent-tools/tools";
---

<Layout
  title="For AI agents"
  description="How this site offers tools to AI agents in your browser, what they can do, and how to turn them off."
>
  <article class="reading">
    <h1>For AI agents</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Some browsers let an AI agent act on a page for you. On those browsers
        this site describes a few tools, so an agent can find and read the
        writing, move around a page, play the narration and run the Python
        examples, instead of guessing from the screen.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every tool uses a control that is already on the page. When an agent
        uses one, the page shows and announces what happened, and you can undo
        it where that makes sense. Tools cannot change the site, download
        models, share anything or change privacy choices. The site sends nothing
        anywhere because of them; what an agent does with what it reads is up to
        the agent you chose.
      </p>
      <h2 id="browser-support">Which browsers</h2>
      <p>
        The tools use{" "}
        <a href="https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/">WebMCP</a>, an
        experimental web standard. Today it works in Chromium browsers where it
        is enabled, such as Chrome with the WebMCP testing flag, and in agents
        built on them. Other browsers ignore it and the site works as usual.
      </p>
      <h2 id="tools">Tools</h2>
      <dl class="agent-tool-list">
        {agentTools.map((tool) => (
          <>
            <dt>
              <code>{tool.name}</code> — {tool.title}
            </dt>
            <dd>{tool.description}</dd>
          </>
        ))}
      </dl>
      <h2 id="turn-off">Turn the tools off</h2>
      <p>
        The setting applies to this browser on this device. It is stored in the
        browser, not sent to the site.
      </p>
      <p>
        <button type="button" data-agent-switch hidden aria-pressed="true">
          Agent tools are on
        </button>
        <noscript>
          The switch needs JavaScript; without it no tools run.
        </noscript>
      </p>
      <p role="status" data-agent-switch-status></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
<script>
  import {
    agentToolsEnabled,
    setAgentToolsEnabled,
  } from "../../runtime/agent-tools/setting";
  const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(
    "[data-agent-switch]",
  )!;
  const status = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(
    "[data-agent-switch-status]",
  )!;
  const render = () => {
    const on = agentToolsEnabled();
    button.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(on));
    button.textContent = on ? "Agent tools are on" : "Agent tools are off";
  };
  button.addEventListener("click", () => {
    const on = !agentToolsEnabled();
    status.textContent = setAgentToolsEnabled(on)
      ? on
        ? "Agent tools turned on for this browser."
        : "Agent tools turned off for this browser."
      : "This browser does not allow saving the setting.";
    render();
  });
  render();
  button.hidden = false;
</script>
<style>
  .agent-tool-list dt {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .agent-tool-list dd {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
  }
</style>
